\begin{slide}
KF'ERROR'VECTOR'UPDATE
\begin{verbatim}
     FUNCTION:

          THIS ROUTINE SUMS THE CUURENT OBSERVATION RESIDUAL
          INTO THE ERROR STATE VECTOR. THE ERROR STATE VECTOR
          IS UPDATED ACCORDING TO:

               EX(ITH) = EX(ITH-1) + K(ITH) * (V(ITH) - A * EX(ITH-1)

          WHERE K(ITH) IS THE ITH KALMAN GAIN, V(ITH) IS THE ITH
          RESIDUAL, "A" THE ITH MEASUREMENT MATRIX AND EX(ITH-1)
          IS THE ERROR STATE VECTOR PRIOR TO THE INCLUSION OF
          THE ITH RESIDUAL. NOTE THAT EX SHALL BE INITIALIZED
          TO ZERO PRIOR TO THE FIRST CALL TI SEVUP. ALSO, V(ITH)
          IS THE CORRECTED OBSERVATION RESIDUAL.


\end{verbatim}
\end{slide}
